# Scoutflo SRE Toolkit: crontab entry for recurring audits.
# Filled in by /scoutflo:schedule-audits. Install via `crontab -e`, verify with `crontab -l`.
#
# Prerequisites on this machine:
#   1. Claude Code installed and authenticated (subscription login, or export
#      ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the env file below). Cron's PATH is minimal: find
#      the absolute binary path with `command -v claude` and use it in the entry.
#   2. ~/.scoutflo/toolkit.yaml filled in (run /scoutflo:connect).
#   3. An env file at ~/.scoutflo/env with `chmod 600`: one export line per
#      *_env variable named in your toolkit.yaml, plus SCOUTFLO_SLACK_WEBHOOK
#      if the brief is enabled. Pull values from your secret manager. Never
#      commit this file anywhere.
#      RECOMMENDED: also add `export SCOUTFLO_AUDIT_DIR="/abs/path/to/scoutflo-audits"`
#      here so the scheduled run writes to the SAME reports directory your
#      interactive runs use — otherwise reports land wherever the `cd` below
#      points, and interactive/scheduled histories can silently diverge.
#
# Notes:
#   - The machine must be awake at the scheduled time; cron does not run missed jobs.
#   - Cost: every run is a headless Claude session; usage scales with the number
#     of configured audits. Weekly is a sane starting cadence.
#   - Reports go to SCOUTFLO_AUDIT_DIR if the env file exports it; otherwise to
#     scoutflo-audits/ under the `cd` directory below. Keep it stable run-to-run
#     so deltas compute automatically. Interactive runs must resolve to the same
#     place (set reports_dir in toolkit.yaml or export SCOUTFLO_AUDIT_DIR there too).
#   - Check ~/.scoutflo/audit-cron.log after the first scheduled run.
#
# Fields: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week
# Example: weekly, Monday 06:00 local time. Tune to your cadence.
# Replace /path/to/your/project and /usr/local/bin/claude (from `command -v claude`).

0 6 * * 1  cd /path/to/your/project && . "$HOME/.scoutflo/env" && /usr/local/bin/claude -p "/scoutflo:audit-all --slack" --allowedTools "Skill,Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep,Bash" >> "$HOME/.scoutflo/audit-cron.log" 2>&1
